IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `uc-core`
IMPORT `uc-core-persons`
IMPORT `uc-core-bodies`
IMPORT `uc3-periods`
IMPORT `uc3-disability-payments`
IMPORT `uc3-sch1-interpretation`
IMPORT `uc3-sch4-interpretation`

-- The Universal Credit Regulations 2013 (S.I. 2013/376), Schedule 4 (housing costs element for renters): the bedrooms a renter is entitled to.
-- Paragraphs 8 to 12 (Part 3, room allocation) and paragraphs 26 to 29 (Part 4, further provisions about size criteria).
-- Source: ../../registers/source-bundle/uksi-2013-376.txt (plain-text rendering, not the official text). Target: the stable build 1.6.98. Layer 1.
--
-- WHY THESE TWO RANGES ARE ONE MODULE. Paragraph 8(2) and paragraph 10(3)(c) name paragraphs 9 to 12 and 26 to 29 together as the
-- provisions that decide the category of accommodation. In a Part 5 calculation only paragraphs 9 to 12 apply (paragraph 8(2)(b)).
--
-- HOW CHILDREN ARE COUNTED (fork U3-F6, U3-F9). Paragraph 10(1)(d) to (f) gives a bedroom to "two children who are under 10", to "two
-- children of the same sex" and to "any other child", and paragraph 10(2) allots a member to whichever description gives the FEWEST
-- bedrooms. The text does not define "sex"; children are therefore counted in four kinds: male or female, under 10 years old or 10 or over.
-- Two children can share a bedroom if both are under 10, or both are of the same sex. The fewest bedrooms for a set of children is found
-- by taking the first child, pairing it with a child of each kind that can share with it in turn, and keeping the smallest total; a child
-- with no possible partner takes a bedroom alone. (Any child who has a possible partner is covered by some largest set of pairs, so
-- only pairings need to be tried.)
--
-- OUT OF RANGE, taken as facts: regulation 4 (responsible for a child), regulation 8 (care leaver), regulation 11 (temporary absence from
-- Great Britain), regulation 19(2), regulation 89(3)(a) (adopter), regulation 98(4) (domestic violence, health care professional,
-- registered social worker). Each is marked "out of range" where it appears.

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Paragraph 9(3): "foster child" is a child in relation to whom the renter (or either joint renter) is a foster parent (regulation 2's definition, the keel's rule).
-- src:2226 | (3) “Foster child” means a child in relation to whom the renter (or either joint renter) is a foster parent.
@ref Sch 4 para 9(3) (src:2226)
DECLARE `Child who may be a foster child` HAS
    child                                                                      IS A BOOLEAN
    `the child's placement with the renter (or either joint renter)`          IS A `Placement of a child with a person`

-- src:2226 | (3) “Foster child” means a child in relation to whom the renter (or either joint renter) is a foster parent.
@ref Sch 4 para 9(3) (src:2226)
GIVEN candidate IS A `Child who may be a foster child`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 4 para 9(3) — foster child` candidate MEANS
    (candidate's child)
    AND (`reg 2 — foster parent` (candidate's `the child's placement with the renter (or either joint renter)`))

-- Paragraph 9(2): a non-dependant is a person who normally lives in the accommodation with the renter and is none of (a) to (g).
-- src:2218 | (2) A person is a non-dependant if the person normally lives in the accommodation with the renter (or joint renters) and is none of the following—
-- src:2219 | (a) a person within sub-paragraph (1)(a) or (b);
-- src:2220 | (b) where the renter is a member of a couple claiming as a single person, the other member of the couple;
-- src:2221 | (c) a foster child;
-- src:2222 | (d) a person who is liable to make payments on a commercial basis in respect of the person's occupation of the accommodation (whether to the renter, joint renters or another person);
-- src:2223 | (e) a person to whom the liability to make relevant payments is owed or a member of their household;
-- src:2224 | (f) a person who has already been treated as a non-dependant in relation to a claim for universal credit by another person liable to make relevant payments in respect of the accommodation occupied by the renter.
-- src:2225 | (g) a child or qualifying young person for whom no-one in the renter’s extended benefit unit is responsible.
@ref Sch 4 para 9(2) (src:2218-2225)
DECLARE `Person who may be a non-dependant` HAS
    `normally lives in the accommodation with the renter (or joint renters)`                                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `a person within sub-paragraph (1)(a) or (b)`                                                                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `where the renter is a member of a couple claiming as a single person, the other member of the couple`        IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person as a possible foster child`                                                                        IS A `Child who may be a foster child`
    `a person who is liable to make payments on a commercial basis in respect of the person's occupation of the accommodation`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `a person to whom the liability to make relevant payments is owed or a member of their household`             IS A BOOLEAN
    `a person who has already been treated as a non-dependant in relation to a claim for universal credit by another person liable to make relevant payments in respect of the accommodation occupied by the renter`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `a child or qualifying young person for whom no-one in the renter's extended benefit unit is responsible`      IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:2219 | (a) a person within sub-paragraph (1)(a) or (b);
-- src:2220 | (b) where the renter is a member of a couple claiming as a single person, the other member of the couple;
-- src:2221 | (c) a foster child;
-- src:2222 | (d) a person who is liable to make payments on a commercial basis in respect of the person's occupation of the accommodation (whether to the renter, joint renters or another person);
-- src:2223 | (e) a person to whom the liability to make relevant payments is owed or a member of their household;
-- src:2224 | (f) a person who has already been treated as a non-dependant in relation to a claim for universal credit by another person liable to make relevant payments in respect of the accommodation occupied by the renter.
-- src:2225 | (g) a child or qualifying young person for whom no-one in the renter’s extended benefit unit is responsible.
@ref Sch 4 para 9(2)(a) to (g) (src:2219-2225)
GIVEN person IS A `Person who may be a non-dependant`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 4 para 9(2) — the descriptions that take a person out of being a non-dependant` person MEANS
    (person's `a person within sub-paragraph (1)(a) or (b)`)
    OR (person's `where the renter is a member of a couple claiming as a single person, the other member of the couple`)
    OR (`Sch 4 para 9(3) — foster child` (person's `the person as a possible foster child`))
    OR (person's `a person who is liable to make payments on a commercial basis in respect of the person's occupation of the accommodation`)
    OR (person's `a person to whom the liability to make relevant payments is owed or a member of their household`)
    OR (person's `a person who has already been treated as a non-dependant in relation to a claim for universal credit by another person liable to make relevant payments in respect of the accommodation occupied by the renter`)
    OR (person's `a child or qualifying young person for whom no-one in the renter's extended benefit unit is responsible`)

-- src:2218 | (2) A person is a non-dependant if the person normally lives in the accommodation with the renter (or joint renters) and is none of the following—
-- src:2219 | (a) a person within sub-paragraph (1)(a) or (b);
-- src:2220 | (b) where the renter is a member of a couple claiming as a single person, the other member of the couple;
-- src:2221 | (c) a foster child;
-- src:2222 | (d) a person who is liable to make payments on a commercial basis in respect of the person's occupation of the accommodation (whether to the renter, joint renters or another person);
-- src:2223 | (e) a person to whom the liability to make relevant payments is owed or a member of their household;
-- src:2224 | (f) a person who has already been treated as a non-dependant in relation to a claim for universal credit by another person liable to make relevant payments in respect of the accommodation occupied by the renter.
-- src:2225 | (g) a child or qualifying young person for whom no-one in the renter’s extended benefit unit is responsible.
@ref Sch 4 para 9(2) (src:2218-2225)
GIVEN person IS A `Person who may be a non-dependant`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 4 para 9(2) — a person is a non-dependant` person MEANS
    (person's `normally lives in the accommodation with the renter (or joint renters)`)
    AND (NOT (`Sch 4 para 9(2) — the descriptions that take a person out of being a non-dependant` person))

-- Paragraph 9(1): the members of the extended benefit unit are the renter (or joint renters), any child or qualifying young person for whom
-- the renter or either joint renter is responsible, and any non-dependant.
-- src:2214 | (1) For the purposes of this Schedule, the members of a renter's extended benefit unit are—
-- src:2215 | (a) the renter (or joint renters);
-- src:2216 | (b) any child or qualifying young person for whom the renter or either joint renter is responsible; and
-- src:2217 | (c) any person who is a non-dependant.
@ref Sch 4 para 9(1) (src:2214-2217)
DECLARE `Person who may be a member of an extended benefit unit` HAS
    `the renter (or one of joint renters)`                                                                  IS A BOOLEAN
    -- out of range: reg 4 (piece uc1), "responsible for a child or qualifying young person"
    `a child or qualifying young person for whom the renter or either joint renter is responsible`        IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person as a possible non-dependant`                                                                IS A `Person who may be a non-dependant`

-- src:2214 | (1) For the purposes of this Schedule, the members of a renter's extended benefit unit are—
-- src:2215 | (a) the renter (or joint renters);
-- src:2216 | (b) any child or qualifying young person for whom the renter or either joint renter is responsible; and
-- src:2217 | (c) any person who is a non-dependant.
@ref Sch 4 para 9(1) (src:2214-2217)
GIVEN person IS A `Person who may be a member of an extended benefit unit`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 4 para 9(1) — a person is a member of the renter's extended benefit unit` person MEANS
    (person's `the renter (or one of joint renters)`)
    OR (person's `a child or qualifying young person for whom the renter or either joint renter is responsible`)
    OR (`Sch 4 para 9(2) — a person is a non-dependant` (person's `the person as a possible non-dependant`))

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Paragraph 11(2): a temporarily absent child or qualifying young person is included in a determination of the number of bedrooms in three cases.
-- "During the first 6 months of the absence" is counted by `uc3 — a day falls within the first months after a start day`.
-- src:2242 | (2) In the case of a child or qualifying young person, the circumstances specified in this sub-paragraph are that the relevant determination relates to any time—
-- src:2243 | (a) during the first 6 months of the absence of a child or qualifying young person for whom the renter is treated as not being responsible in accordance with regulation 4(6)(a) (child or qualifying young person looked after by local authority) where, immediately before the local authority started looking after them, the child or qualifying young person was included in the renter's extended benefit unit and the renter's award included the housing costs element;
-- src:2244 | (b) during the first 6 months of the absence of a child or qualifying young person for whom the renter is treated as not being responsible in accordance with regulation 4(6)(b) (child or qualifying young person is a prisoner) where—
-- src:2245 | (i) immediately before becoming a prisoner, the child or qualifying young person was included in the renter's extended benefit unit and the renter's award included the housing costs element, and
-- src:2246 | (ii) the child or qualifying young person has not been sentenced to a term in custody that is expected to extend beyond that 6 months; or
-- src:2247 | (c) before the renter or joint renter ceases to be responsible for a temporarily absent child or qualifying young person in accordance with regulation 4(7) (absence exceeding specified duration).
@ref Sch 4 para 11(2) (src:2242-2247)
DECLARE `Temporarily absent child or qualifying young person` HAS
    `day to which the determination relates`                                           IS A DATE
    `first day of the absence`                                                         IS A DATE
    -- out of range: reg 4(6)(a) (piece uc1), a child or qualifying young person looked after by a local authority
    `the renter is treated as not being responsible for the child or qualifying young person in accordance with regulation 4(6)(a)`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `immediately before the local authority started looking after them the child or qualifying young person was included in the renter's extended benefit unit and the renter's award included the housing costs element`  IS A BOOLEAN
    -- out of range: reg 4(6)(b) (piece uc1), a child or qualifying young person who is a prisoner
    `the renter is treated as not being responsible for the child or qualifying young person in accordance with regulation 4(6)(b)`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `immediately before becoming a prisoner the child or qualifying young person was included in the renter's extended benefit unit and the renter's award included the housing costs element`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the child or qualifying young person has not been sentenced to a term in custody that is expected to extend beyond that 6 months`  IS A BOOLEAN
    -- out of range: reg 4(7) (piece uc1), absence exceeding the specified duration
    `the determination relates to a time before the renter or joint renter ceases to be responsible for the temporarily absent child or qualifying young person in accordance with regulation 4(7)`  IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:2243 | (a) during the first 6 months of the absence of a child or qualifying young person for whom the renter is treated as not being responsible in accordance with regulation 4(6)(a) (child or qualifying young person looked after by local authority) where, immediately before the local authority started looking after them, the child or qualifying young person was included in the renter's extended benefit unit and the renter's award included the housing costs element;
@ref Sch 4 para 11(2)(a) (src:2243)
GIVEN absent IS A `Temporarily absent child or qualifying young person`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 4 para 11(2)(a) — looked after by a local authority` absent MEANS
    (`uc3 — a day falls within the first months after a start day` (absent's `day to which the determination relates`) (absent's `first day of the absence`) 6)
    AND (absent's `the renter is treated as not being responsible for the child or qualifying young person in accordance with regulation 4(6)(a)`)
    AND (absent's `immediately before the local authority started looking after them the child or qualifying young person was included in the renter's extended benefit unit and the renter's award included the housing costs element`)

-- src:2244 | (b) during the first 6 months of the absence of a child or qualifying young person for whom the renter is treated as not being responsible in accordance with regulation 4(6)(b) (child or qualifying young person is a prisoner) where—
-- src:2245 | (i) immediately before becoming a prisoner, the child or qualifying young person was included in the renter's extended benefit unit and the renter's award included the housing costs element, and
-- src:2246 | (ii) the child or qualifying young person has not been sentenced to a term in custody that is expected to extend beyond that 6 months; or
@ref Sch 4 para 11(2)(b) (src:2244-2246)
GIVEN absent IS A `Temporarily absent child or qualifying young person`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 4 para 11(2)(b) — a prisoner` absent MEANS
    (`uc3 — a day falls within the first months after a start day` (absent's `day to which the determination relates`) (absent's `first day of the absence`) 6)
    AND (absent's `the renter is treated as not being responsible for the child or qualifying young person in accordance with regulation 4(6)(b)`)
    AND (absent's `immediately before becoming a prisoner the child or qualifying young person was included in the renter's extended benefit unit and the renter's award included the housing costs element`)
    AND (absent's `the child or qualifying young person has not been sentenced to a term in custody that is expected to extend beyond that 6 months`)

-- src:2247 | (c) before the renter or joint renter ceases to be responsible for a temporarily absent child or qualifying young person in accordance with regulation 4(7) (absence exceeding specified duration).
@ref Sch 4 para 11(2)(c) (src:2247)
GIVEN absent IS A `Temporarily absent child or qualifying young person`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 4 para 11(2)(c) — before responsibility ceases under regulation 4(7)` absent MEANS
    absent's `the determination relates to a time before the renter or joint renter ceases to be responsible for the temporarily absent child or qualifying young person in accordance with regulation 4(7)`

-- src:2242 | (2) In the case of a child or qualifying young person, the circumstances specified in this sub-paragraph are that the relevant determination relates to any time—
-- src:2243 | (a) during the first 6 months of the absence of a child or qualifying young person for whom the renter is treated as not being responsible in accordance with regulation 4(6)(a) (child or qualifying young person looked after by local authority) where, immediately before the local authority started looking after them, the child or qualifying young person was included in the renter's extended benefit unit and the renter's award included the housing costs element;
-- src:2244 | (b) during the first 6 months of the absence of a child or qualifying young person for whom the renter is treated as not being responsible in accordance with regulation 4(6)(b) (child or qualifying young person is a prisoner) where—
-- src:2245 | (i) immediately before becoming a prisoner, the child or qualifying young person was included in the renter's extended benefit unit and the renter's award included the housing costs element, and
-- src:2246 | (ii) the child or qualifying young person has not been sentenced to a term in custody that is expected to extend beyond that 6 months; or
-- src:2247 | (c) before the renter or joint renter ceases to be responsible for a temporarily absent child or qualifying young person in accordance with regulation 4(7) (absence exceeding specified duration).
@ref Sch 4 para 11(2) (src:2242-2247)
GIVEN absent IS A `Temporarily absent child or qualifying young person`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 4 para 11(2) — a temporarily absent child or qualifying young person is included` absent MEANS
    (`Sch 4 para 11(2)(a) — looked after by a local authority` absent)
    OR (`Sch 4 para 11(2)(b) — a prisoner` absent)
    OR (`Sch 4 para 11(2)(c) — before responsibility ceases under regulation 4(7)` absent)

-- Paragraph 11(3): a temporarily absent renter is included while the absence from Great Britain is disregarded, or while the renter is a
-- prisoner to whom regulation 19(2) applies. Both are regulation 11 and regulation 19 (uc1), taken as facts.
-- src:2248 | (3) In the case of a renter, the circumstances specified in this sub-paragraph are that the relevant determination relates to any time when—
-- src:2249 | (a) the temporary absence from Great Britain of the renter is disregarded in accordance with regulation 11(1) or (2); or
-- src:2250 | (b) the renter is a prisoner to whom regulation 19(2) (existing award includes housing costs when person becomes a prisoner) applies.
@ref Sch 4 para 11(3) (src:2248-2250)
DECLARE `Temporarily absent renter` HAS
    -- out of range: reg 11(1) and (2) (piece uc1)
    `the temporary absence from Great Britain of the renter is disregarded in accordance with regulation 11(1) or (2)`  IS A BOOLEAN
    -- out of range: reg 19(2) (piece uc1)
    `the renter is a prisoner to whom regulation 19(2) applies`                                                        IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:2248 | (3) In the case of a renter, the circumstances specified in this sub-paragraph are that the relevant determination relates to any time when—
-- src:2249 | (a) the temporary absence from Great Britain of the renter is disregarded in accordance with regulation 11(1) or (2); or
-- src:2250 | (b) the renter is a prisoner to whom regulation 19(2) (existing award includes housing costs when person becomes a prisoner) applies.
@ref Sch 4 para 11(3) (src:2248-2250)
GIVEN absent IS A `Temporarily absent renter`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 4 para 11(3) — a temporarily absent renter is included` absent MEANS
    (absent's `the temporary absence from Great Britain of the renter is disregarded in accordance with regulation 11(1) or (2)`)
    OR (absent's `the renter is a prisoner to whom regulation 19(2) applies`)

-- Paragraphs 11(4) and (5): a temporarily absent non-dependant is included during four kinds of period.
-- (a) the first month of an absence from Great Britain, and a further month if the circumstances are those of regulation 11(2) (death of a close relative);
-- (b) the first 6 months of an absence from Great Britain in the circumstances of regulation 11(3)(a) (treatment for illness or impairment);
-- (c) the first 6 months as a prisoner not sentenced to a term expected to extend beyond that 6 months;
-- (d) any period in which a son, daughter, step-son or step-daughter of the renter is a member of the armed forces away on operations.
-- Paragraph 11(4)(b) adds, for periods (a) to (c), that the non-dependant was in the extended benefit unit just before the period and that
-- the award included the housing costs element; for period (d) only the first of those.
-- src:2251 | (4) In the case of a non-dependant, the circumstances specified in this sub-paragraph are that—
-- src:2252 | (a) the relevant determination relates to any time during a period specified in sub-paragraph (5); and
-- src:2253 | (b) immediately before the start of that period, the non-dependant was included in the renter's extended benefit unit and , in the circumstances specified in sub-paragraph (5) (a) to (c), the renter's award included the housing costs element.
-- src:2254 | (5) The specified periods are—
-- src:2255 | (a) the first month of the non-dependant's temporary absence from Great Britain and, if the circumstances of the non-dependant are such as would be disregarded for the purposes of regulation 11(2) (death of a close relative), a further one month;
-- src:2256 | (b) the first 6 months of the non-dependant's temporary absence from Great Britain in the circumstances described in regulation 11(3)(a) (absence solely in connection with treatment for illness or physical or mental impairment);
-- src:2257 | (c) the first 6 months that the non-dependant is a prisoner where the non-dependant has not been sentenced to a term in custody that is expected to extend beyond that 6 months.
-- src:2258 | (d) any period during which a non-dependant who is the son, daughter, step-son or step-daughter of a renter or joint renters is a member of the armed forces away on operations.
@ref Sch 4 para 11(4) and (5) (src:2251-2258)
DECLARE `Temporarily absent non-dependant` HAS
    `day to which the determination relates`                                                                                       IS A DATE
    `first day of the absence`                                                                                                     IS A DATE
    `the absence is a temporary absence from Great Britain`                                                                        IS A BOOLEAN
    -- out of range: reg 11(2) (piece uc1), death of a close relative
    `the circumstances of the non-dependant are such as would be disregarded for the purposes of regulation 11(2)`                  IS A BOOLEAN
    -- out of range: reg 11(3)(a) (piece uc1), absence solely in connection with treatment for illness or physical or mental impairment
    `the absence from Great Britain is in the circumstances described in regulation 11(3)(a)`                                      IS A BOOLEAN
    `the non-dependant is a prisoner`                                                                                              IS A BOOLEAN
    `the non-dependant has not been sentenced to a term in custody that is expected to extend beyond that 6 months`                IS A BOOLEAN
    `the non-dependant is the son, daughter, step-son or step-daughter of a renter or joint renters`                               IS A BOOLEAN
    `the non-dependant is a member of the armed forces away on operations`                                                         IS A BOOLEAN
    `immediately before the start of the period the non-dependant was included in the renter's extended benefit unit`              IS A BOOLEAN
    `immediately before the start of the period the renter's award included the housing costs element`                             IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:2255 | (a) the first month of the non-dependant's temporary absence from Great Britain and, if the circumstances of the non-dependant are such as would be disregarded for the purposes of regulation 11(2) (death of a close relative), a further one month;
@ref Sch 4 para 11(5)(a) (src:2255)
GIVEN absent IS A `Temporarily absent non-dependant`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 4 para 11(5)(a) — the first month of an absence from Great Britain, and a further month` absent MEANS
    (absent's `the absence is a temporary absence from Great Britain`)
    AND (    (`uc3 — a day falls within the first months after a start day` (absent's `day to which the determination relates`) (absent's `first day of the absence`) 1)
          OR (    (absent's `the circumstances of the non-dependant are such as would be disregarded for the purposes of regulation 11(2)`)
              AND (`uc3 — a day falls within the first months after a start day` (absent's `day to which the determination relates`) (absent's `first day of the absence`) 2)))

-- src:2256 | (b) the first 6 months of the non-dependant's temporary absence from Great Britain in the circumstances described in regulation 11(3)(a) (absence solely in connection with treatment for illness or physical or mental impairment);
@ref Sch 4 para 11(5)(b) (src:2256)
GIVEN absent IS A `Temporarily absent non-dependant`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 4 para 11(5)(b) — the first 6 months of an absence for treatment` absent MEANS
    (absent's `the absence from Great Britain is in the circumstances described in regulation 11(3)(a)`)
    AND (`uc3 — a day falls within the first months after a start day` (absent's `day to which the determination relates`) (absent's `first day of the absence`) 6)

-- src:2257 | (c) the first 6 months that the non-dependant is a prisoner where the non-dependant has not been sentenced to a term in custody that is expected to extend beyond that 6 months.
@ref Sch 4 para 11(5)(c) (src:2257)
GIVEN absent IS A `Temporarily absent non-dependant`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 4 para 11(5)(c) — the first 6 months as a prisoner` absent MEANS
    (absent's `the non-dependant is a prisoner`)
    AND (absent's `the non-dependant has not been sentenced to a term in custody that is expected to extend beyond that 6 months`)
    AND (`uc3 — a day falls within the first months after a start day` (absent's `day to which the determination relates`) (absent's `first day of the absence`) 6)

-- src:2258 | (d) any period during which a non-dependant who is the son, daughter, step-son or step-daughter of a renter or joint renters is a member of the armed forces away on operations.
@ref Sch 4 para 11(5)(d) (src:2258)
GIVEN absent IS A `Temporarily absent non-dependant`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 4 para 11(5)(d) — a son or daughter in the armed forces away on operations` absent MEANS
    (absent's `the non-dependant is the son, daughter, step-son or step-daughter of a renter or joint renters`)
    AND (absent's `the non-dependant is a member of the armed forces away on operations`)

-- src:2251 | (4) In the case of a non-dependant, the circumstances specified in this sub-paragraph are that—
-- src:2252 | (a) the relevant determination relates to any time during a period specified in sub-paragraph (5); and
-- src:2253 | (b) immediately before the start of that period, the non-dependant was included in the renter's extended benefit unit and , in the circumstances specified in sub-paragraph (5) (a) to (c), the renter's award included the housing costs element.
-- src:2254 | (5) The specified periods are—
-- src:2255 | (a) the first month of the non-dependant's temporary absence from Great Britain and, if the circumstances of the non-dependant are such as would be disregarded for the purposes of regulation 11(2) (death of a close relative), a further one month;
-- src:2256 | (b) the first 6 months of the non-dependant's temporary absence from Great Britain in the circumstances described in regulation 11(3)(a) (absence solely in connection with treatment for illness or physical or mental impairment);
-- src:2257 | (c) the first 6 months that the non-dependant is a prisoner where the non-dependant has not been sentenced to a term in custody that is expected to extend beyond that 6 months.
-- src:2258 | (d) any period during which a non-dependant who is the son, daughter, step-son or step-daughter of a renter or joint renters is a member of the armed forces away on operations.
@ref Sch 4 para 11(4) (src:2251-2258)
GIVEN absent IS A `Temporarily absent non-dependant`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 4 para 11(4) — a temporarily absent non-dependant is included` absent MEANS
    (absent's `immediately before the start of the period the non-dependant was included in the renter's extended benefit unit`)
    AND (    (    ((`Sch 4 para 11(5)(a) — the first month of an absence from Great Britain, and a further month` absent)
                  OR (`Sch 4 para 11(5)(b) — the first 6 months of an absence for treatment` absent)
                  OR (`Sch 4 para 11(5)(c) — the first 6 months as a prisoner` absent))
              AND (absent's `immediately before the start of the period the renter's award included the housing costs element`))
          OR (`Sch 4 para 11(5)(d) — a son or daughter in the armed forces away on operations` absent))

-- Paragraph 11(6): a non-dependant absent in circumstances other than those of (4) and (5) is not treated as a member if the absence exceeds,
-- or is expected to exceed, 6 months. The answer TRUE means that the non-dependant is NOT treated as a member of the extended benefit unit.
-- src:2259 | (6) Any non-dependant who is temporarily absent from the accommodation occupied by the renter in circumstances other than those specified in sub-paragraphs (4) and (5) is not to be treated as being a member of the renter's extended benefit unit if that absence exceeds, or is expected to exceed, 6 months.
@ref Sch 4 para 11(6) (src:2259)
DECLARE `Non-dependant absent in other circumstances` HAS
    `the absence is in circumstances other than those specified in sub-paragraphs (4) and (5)`      IS A BOOLEAN
    `first day of the absence`                                                                      IS A DATE
    `day to which the determination relates`                                                        IS A DATE
    `last day to which the absence is expected to last`                                             IS A DATE

-- src:2259 | (6) Any non-dependant who is temporarily absent from the accommodation occupied by the renter in circumstances other than those specified in sub-paragraphs (4) and (5) is not to be treated as being a member of the renter's extended benefit unit if that absence exceeds, or is expected to exceed, 6 months.
@ref Sch 4 para 11(6) (src:2259)
GIVEN absent IS A `Non-dependant absent in other circumstances`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 4 para 11(6) — an absent non-dependant is not treated as a member of the extended benefit unit` absent MEANS
    (absent's `the absence is in circumstances other than those specified in sub-paragraphs (4) and (5)`)
    AND (    (`uc3 — a period lasting to a last day exceeds a number of months` (absent's `first day of the absence`) (absent's `day to which the determination relates`) 6)
          OR (`uc3 — a period lasting to a last day exceeds a number of months` (absent's `first day of the absence`) (absent's `last day to which the absence is expected to last`) 6))

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Paragraph 12(3): the overnight care condition, for one person.
-- src:2271 | (3) A person satisfies the overnight care condition if—
-- src:2272 | (a) they are in receipt of—
-- src:2273 | (i) the care component of disability living allowance at the middle or highest rate;
-- src:2274 | (ia) the care component of child disability payment at the middle or highest rate in accordance with regulation 11(5) of the DACYP Regulations;
-- src:2275 | (ib) the care component of Scottish adult disability living allowance at the highest or middle rate in accordance with regulation 6(4) of the Disability Assistance (Scottish Adult Disability Living Allowance) Regulations 2025;
-- src:2276 | (ii) attendance allowance; ...
-- src:2277 | (iia) pension age disability payment;
-- src:2278 | (iii) the daily living component of personal independence payment or;
-- src:2279 | (iv) the daily living component of adult disability payment at the standard or enhanced rate;
-- src:2280 | (b) one or more persons who do not live in the renter’s accommodation are engaged to provide overnight care for the person and to stay overnight in the accommodation on a regular basis; and
-- src:2281 | (c) overnight care is provided under arrangements entered into for that purpose.
@ref Sch 4 para 12(3) (src:2271-2281)
DECLARE `Person who may satisfy the overnight care condition` HAS
    payments                                                                                       IS A `Disability payments of a person`
    `one or more persons who do not live in the renter's accommodation are engaged to provide overnight care for the person and to stay overnight in the accommodation on a regular basis`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `overnight care is provided under arrangements entered into for that purpose`                  IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:2271 | (3) A person satisfies the overnight care condition if—
-- src:2272 | (a) they are in receipt of—
-- src:2273 | (i) the care component of disability living allowance at the middle or highest rate;
-- src:2274 | (ia) the care component of child disability payment at the middle or highest rate in accordance with regulation 11(5) of the DACYP Regulations;
-- src:2275 | (ib) the care component of Scottish adult disability living allowance at the highest or middle rate in accordance with regulation 6(4) of the Disability Assistance (Scottish Adult Disability Living Allowance) Regulations 2025;
-- src:2276 | (ii) attendance allowance; ...
-- src:2277 | (iia) pension age disability payment;
-- src:2278 | (iii) the daily living component of personal independence payment or;
-- src:2279 | (iv) the daily living component of adult disability payment at the standard or enhanced rate;
-- src:2280 | (b) one or more persons who do not live in the renter’s accommodation are engaged to provide overnight care for the person and to stay overnight in the accommodation on a regular basis; and
-- src:2281 | (c) overnight care is provided under arrangements entered into for that purpose.
@ref Sch 4 para 12(3) (src:2271-2281)
GIVEN person IS A `Person who may satisfy the overnight care condition`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 4 para 12(3) — a person satisfies the overnight care condition` person MEANS
    (`Sch 3 para 5(3)(b) — a person in receipt of one of the listed payments` (person's payments))
    AND (person's `one or more persons who do not live in the renter's accommodation are engaged to provide overnight care for the person and to stay overnight in the accommodation on a regular basis`)
    AND (person's `overnight care is provided under arrangements entered into for that purpose`)

-- Paragraph 12(A1): the persons who may satisfy the overnight care condition are the renter, a person in the renter's extended benefit unit
-- and a child in respect of whom the renter satisfies the foster parent condition; the list holds each such person asked about.
-- src:2261 | (A1) A renter is entitled to an additional bedroom if one or more of the following persons satisfies the overnight care condition (see sub-paragraph (3))—
-- src:2262 | (a) the renter;
-- src:2263 | (b) a person in the renter’s extended benefit unit;
-- src:2264 | (c) a child in respect of whom the renter satisfies the foster parent condition (see sub-paragraphs (4) and (5)).
@ref Sch 4 para 12(A1) (src:2261-2264)
GIVEN persons IS A LIST OF `Person who may satisfy the overnight care condition`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 4 para 12(A1) — one or more of the persons listed satisfies the overnight care condition` persons MEANS
    any `Sch 4 para 12(3) — a person satisfies the overnight care condition` persons

-- Paragraphs 12(4) and (5): the foster parent condition. A foster parent (regulation 2's definition) or an adopter with whom a child has been
-- placed for adoption; "foster parent" includes a person who would be one but for having no child placed with them at present, if no more
-- than 12 months have passed since the last placement ended (or since approval, if none has yet been made).
-- src:2282 | (4) A renter satisfies the foster parent condition if the renter is—
-- src:2283 | (a) a foster parent; or
-- src:2284 | (b) an adopter with whom a child has been placed for adoption.
-- src:2285 | (5) For the purposes of sub-paragraph (4) “foster parent” includes a person who would be a foster parent, but for the fact that they do not currently have any child placed with them, provided that any period since the date when their last placement ended (or, if they have not yet had a child placed with them, since the date when they were approved to be a foster parent) does not exceed 12 months.
@ref Sch 4 para 12(4) and (5) (src:2282-2285)
DECLARE `Renter who may satisfy the foster parent condition` HAS
    `the renter's placement of a child`                                                                                    IS A `Placement of a child with a person`
    `the renter would be a foster parent but for the fact that they do not currently have any child placed with them`     IS A BOOLEAN
    `the day the renter's last placement ended or, if no child has yet been placed with them, the day on which they were approved to be a foster parent`  IS A DATE
    `day to which the determination relates`                                                                               IS A DATE
    -- out of range: reg 89(3)(a) (piece uc4), "adopter"
    `adopter with whom a child has been placed for adoption`                                                               IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:2285 | (5) For the purposes of sub-paragraph (4) “foster parent” includes a person who would be a foster parent, but for the fact that they do not currently have any child placed with them, provided that any period since the date when their last placement ended (or, if they have not yet had a child placed with them, since the date when they were approved to be a foster parent) does not exceed 12 months.
@ref Sch 4 para 12(5) (src:2285)
GIVEN renter IS A `Renter who may satisfy the foster parent condition`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 4 para 12(5) — a person who would be a foster parent but for having no child placed` renter MEANS
    (renter's `the renter would be a foster parent but for the fact that they do not currently have any child placed with them`)
    AND (NOT (`uc3 — a period lasting to a last day exceeds a number of months` (renter's `the day the renter's last placement ended or, if no child has yet been placed with them, the day on which they were approved to be a foster parent`) (renter's `day to which the determination relates`) 12))

-- src:2282 | (4) A renter satisfies the foster parent condition if the renter is—
-- src:2283 | (a) a foster parent; or
-- src:2284 | (b) an adopter with whom a child has been placed for adoption.
-- src:2285 | (5) For the purposes of sub-paragraph (4) “foster parent” includes a person who would be a foster parent, but for the fact that they do not currently have any child placed with them, provided that any period since the date when their last placement ended (or, if they have not yet had a child placed with them, since the date when they were approved to be a foster parent) does not exceed 12 months.
@ref Sch 4 para 12(4) (src:2282-2284)
GIVEN renter IS A `Renter who may satisfy the foster parent condition`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 4 para 12(4) — a renter satisfies the foster parent condition` renter MEANS
    (`reg 2 — foster parent` (renter's `the renter's placement of a child`))
    OR (`Sch 4 para 12(5) — a person who would be a foster parent but for having no child placed` renter)
    OR (renter's `adopter with whom a child has been placed for adoption`)

-- Paragraph 12(6): the disabled child condition, for one child: in receipt of the care component of disability living allowance or of child
-- disability payment at the middle or highest rate (the keel's list is in uc3-disability-payments), and by virtue of disability not reasonably
-- able to share a room with another child. "Would (but for the provisions of this paragraph) be expected to share a bedroom" is not a fact
-- about the child alone: it depends on how the children are allotted, and is worked out in paragraph 12(8) below.
-- src:2286 | (6) A renter satisfies the disabled child condition if they or another member of their extended benefit unit are responsible for a child who would (but for the provisions of this paragraph) be expected to share a bedroom and that child is—
-- src:2287 | (a) in receipt of—
-- src:2288 | (i) the care component of disability living allowance at the middle or highest rate; or
-- src:2289 | (ii) the care component of child disability payment at the middle or highest rate in accordance with regulation 11(5) of the DACYP Regulations; and
-- src:2290 | (b) by virtue of their disability, not reasonably able to share a room with another child.
@ref Sch 4 para 12(6) (src:2286-2290)
DECLARE `Child who may satisfy the disabled child condition` HAS
    payments                                                                                                  IS A `Disability payments of a person`
    `by virtue of their disability, the child is not reasonably able to share a room with another child`     IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:2287 | (a) in receipt of—
-- src:2288 | (i) the care component of disability living allowance at the middle or highest rate; or
-- src:2289 | (ii) the care component of child disability payment at the middle or highest rate in accordance with regulation 11(5) of the DACYP Regulations; and
-- src:2290 | (b) by virtue of their disability, not reasonably able to share a room with another child.
@ref Sch 4 para 12(6)(a) and (b) (src:2287-2290)
GIVEN child IS A `Child who may satisfy the disabled child condition`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 4 para 12(6)(a) and (b) — a child in receipt of a listed care component who cannot share a room` child MEANS
    (`Sch 4 para 12(6)(a) — a child in receipt of one of the listed care components` (child's payments))
    AND (child's `by virtue of their disability, the child is not reasonably able to share a room with another child`)

-- Paragraph 12(6A): the disabled person condition, for one renter.
-- src:2291 | (6A) A renter satisfies the disabled person condition if they would (but for the provisions of this paragraph) be expected to share a bedroom with a joint renter and—
-- src:2292 | (a) the renter is in receipt of—
-- src:2293 | (i) the care component of disability living allowance at the middle or highest rate;
-- src:2294 | (ia) the care component of child disability payment at the middle or highest rate in accordance with regulation 11(5) of the DACYP Regulations;
-- src:2295 | (ib) the care component of Scottish adult disability living allowance at the highest or middle rate in accordance with regulation 6(4) of the Disability Assistance (Scottish Adult Disability Living Allowance) Regulations 2025;
-- src:2296 | (ii) attendance allowance ...;
-- src:2297 | (iia) pension age disability payment ...;
-- src:2298 | (iii) the daily living component of personal independence payment; ...
-- src:2299 | (iv) the daily living component of adult disability payment at the standard or enhanced rate; and
-- src:2300 | (b) the renter is, by virtue of their disability, not reasonably able to share a bedroom with the joint renter.
@ref Sch 4 para 12(6A) (src:2291-2300)
DECLARE `Renter who may satisfy the disabled person condition` HAS
    `the renter would, but for the provisions of this paragraph, be expected to share a bedroom with a joint renter`      IS A BOOLEAN
    payments                                                                                                              IS A `Disability payments of a person`
    `by virtue of their disability, the renter is not reasonably able to share a bedroom with the joint renter`           IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:2291 | (6A) A renter satisfies the disabled person condition if they would (but for the provisions of this paragraph) be expected to share a bedroom with a joint renter and—
-- src:2292 | (a) the renter is in receipt of—
-- src:2293 | (i) the care component of disability living allowance at the middle or highest rate;
-- src:2294 | (ia) the care component of child disability payment at the middle or highest rate in accordance with regulation 11(5) of the DACYP Regulations;
-- src:2295 | (ib) the care component of Scottish adult disability living allowance at the highest or middle rate in accordance with regulation 6(4) of the Disability Assistance (Scottish Adult Disability Living Allowance) Regulations 2025;
-- src:2296 | (ii) attendance allowance ...;
-- src:2297 | (iia) pension age disability payment ...;
-- src:2298 | (iii) the daily living component of personal independence payment; ...
-- src:2299 | (iv) the daily living component of adult disability payment at the standard or enhanced rate; and
-- src:2300 | (b) the renter is, by virtue of their disability, not reasonably able to share a bedroom with the joint renter.
@ref Sch 4 para 12(6A) (src:2291-2300)
GIVEN renter IS A `Renter who may satisfy the disabled person condition`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 4 para 12(6A) — a renter satisfies the disabled person condition` renter MEANS
    (renter's `the renter would, but for the provisions of this paragraph, be expected to share a bedroom with a joint renter`)
    AND (`Sch 3 para 5(3)(b) — a person in receipt of one of the listed payments` (renter's payments))
    AND (renter's `by virtue of their disability, the renter is not reasonably able to share a bedroom with the joint renter`)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Children in the extended benefit unit, in four kinds (see the note at the top of this module).
-- src:2232 | (d) two children who are under 10 years old;
-- src:2233 | (e) two children of the same sex;
-- src:2234 | (f) any other child.
@ref Sch 4 para 10(1)(d) to (f) (src:2232-2234)
DECLARE `Children in a renter's extended benefit unit` HAS
    `male children under 10 years old`        IS A NUMBER
    `female children under 10 years old`      IS A NUMBER
    `male children aged 10 or over`           IS A NUMBER
    `female children aged 10 or over`         IS A NUMBER

-- The fewest bedrooms for children of four kinds, with a, b, c, d the numbers of male children under 10, female children under 10, male children
-- aged 10 or over and female children aged 10 or over. Two children may share if both are under 10 or both are of the same sex. The first
-- child that is left is paired with each kind of child that may share with it, in turn; a child with no possible partner has a bedroom alone.
-- The bedroom count of a pairing is never worse than that of leaving the child alone when it has a partner (see the note at the top).
-- src:2232 | (d) two children who are under 10 years old;
-- src:2233 | (e) two children of the same sex;
-- src:2234 | (f) any other child.
-- src:2235 | (2) A member of the extended benefit unit to whom two or more of the descriptions in sub-paragraph (1) apply is to be allotted to whichever description results in the renter being entitled to the fewest bedrooms.
@ref Sch 4 para 10(1)(d) to (f) and (2) (src:2232-2235)
GIVEN a IS A NUMBER
      b IS A NUMBER
      c IS A NUMBER
      d IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Sch 4 para 10(2) — the fewest bedrooms for children of four kinds` a b c d MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF a AT LEAST 1 THEN 1 PLUS (IF (a AT LEAST 2) OR (b AT LEAST 1) OR (c AT LEAST 1) THEN min (min (IF a AT LEAST 2 THEN `Sch 4 para 10(2) — the fewest bedrooms for children of four kinds` (a MINUS 2) b c d ELSE 1000) (IF b AT LEAST 1 THEN `Sch 4 para 10(2) — the fewest bedrooms for children of four kinds` (a MINUS 1) (b MINUS 1) c d ELSE 1000)) (IF c AT LEAST 1 THEN `Sch 4 para 10(2) — the fewest bedrooms for children of four kinds` (a MINUS 1) b (c MINUS 1) d ELSE 1000) ELSE `Sch 4 para 10(2) — the fewest bedrooms for children of four kinds` (a MINUS 1) b c d)
        IF b AT LEAST 1 THEN 1 PLUS (IF (b AT LEAST 2) OR (d AT LEAST 1) THEN min (IF b AT LEAST 2 THEN `Sch 4 para 10(2) — the fewest bedrooms for children of four kinds` a (b MINUS 2) c d ELSE 1000) (IF d AT LEAST 1 THEN `Sch 4 para 10(2) — the fewest bedrooms for children of four kinds` a (b MINUS 1) c (d MINUS 1) ELSE 1000) ELSE `Sch 4 para 10(2) — the fewest bedrooms for children of four kinds` a (b MINUS 1) c d)
        IF c AT LEAST 1 THEN 1 PLUS (IF c AT LEAST 2 THEN `Sch 4 para 10(2) — the fewest bedrooms for children of four kinds` a b (c MINUS 2) d ELSE `Sch 4 para 10(2) — the fewest bedrooms for children of four kinds` a b (c MINUS 1) d)
        IF d AT LEAST 1 THEN 1 PLUS (IF d AT LEAST 2 THEN `Sch 4 para 10(2) — the fewest bedrooms for children of four kinds` a b c (d MINUS 2) ELSE `Sch 4 para 10(2) — the fewest bedrooms for children of four kinds` a b c (d MINUS 1))
        OTHERWISE 0

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- The fewest bedrooms for a whole group of children, and the number of children in it.
-- src:2232 | (d) two children who are under 10 years old;
-- src:2233 | (e) two children of the same sex;
-- src:2234 | (f) any other child.
-- src:2235 | (2) A member of the extended benefit unit to whom two or more of the descriptions in sub-paragraph (1) apply is to be allotted to whichever description results in the renter being entitled to the fewest bedrooms.
@ref Sch 4 para 10(1)(d) to (f) and (2) (src:2232-2235)
GIVEN group IS A `Children in a renter's extended benefit unit`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Sch 4 para 10(2) — the fewest bedrooms for a group of children` group MEANS
    `Sch 4 para 10(2) — the fewest bedrooms for children of four kinds` (group's `male children under 10 years old`) (group's `female children under 10 years old`) (group's `male children aged 10 or over`) (group's `female children aged 10 or over`)

-- src:2232 | (d) two children who are under 10 years old;
-- src:2233 | (e) two children of the same sex;
-- src:2234 | (f) any other child.
@ref Sch 4 para 10(1)(d) to (f) (src:2232-2234)
GIVEN group IS A `Children in a renter's extended benefit unit`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Sch 4 para 10(1)(d) to (f) — the number of children in a group` group MEANS
    (group's `male children under 10 years old`) PLUS (group's `female children under 10 years old`) PLUS (group's `male children aged 10 or over`) PLUS (group's `female children aged 10 or over`)

-- The group of children that is left when the children with the disabled child condition are taken out (kind by kind; never below nil).
-- src:2302 | (8) Where a renter, or one or both of joint renters, satisfy the disabled child condition in relation to one or more children, they are entitled to as many additional bedrooms as are necessary to ensure that each such child has their own bedroom.
@ref Sch 4 para 12(8) (src:2302)
GIVEN group IS A `Children in a renter's extended benefit unit`
      disabled IS A `Children in a renter's extended benefit unit`
GIVETH A `Children in a renter's extended benefit unit`
`Sch 4 para 12(8) — the children who are left when the children with the disabled child condition are taken out` group disabled MEANS
    `Children in a renter's extended benefit unit` WITH
        `male children under 10 years old` IS max 0 ((group's `male children under 10 years old`) MINUS (disabled's `male children under 10 years old`))
        `female children under 10 years old` IS max 0 ((group's `female children under 10 years old`) MINUS (disabled's `female children under 10 years old`))
        `male children aged 10 or over` IS max 0 ((group's `male children aged 10 or over`) MINUS (disabled's `male children aged 10 or over`))
        `female children aged 10 or over` IS max 0 ((group's `female children aged 10 or over`) MINUS (disabled's `female children aged 10 or over`))

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- The members of the extended benefit unit as the size criteria count them, after paragraph 11 has decided who is included.
-- "Disabled children" are those children who are in receipt of a listed care component and by virtue of their disability not reasonably
-- able to share a room (paragraph 12(6)(a) and (b)); they are counted again in "children".
-- src:2228 | (1) A renter is entitled to one bedroom for each of the following categories of persons in their extended benefit unit—
-- src:2229 | (a) the renter (or joint renters);
-- src:2230 | (b) a qualifying young person for whom the renter or either joint renter is responsible;
-- src:2231 | (c) a non-dependant who is not a child;
-- src:2232 | (d) two children who are under 10 years old;
-- src:2233 | (e) two children of the same sex;
-- src:2234 | (f) any other child.
@ref Sch 4 para 10(1) (src:2228-2234)
DECLARE `Extended benefit unit for the size criteria` HAS
    `qualifying young persons for whom the renter or either joint renter is responsible`                IS A NUMBER
    `non-dependants who are not children`                                                              IS A NUMBER
    children                                                                                           IS A `Children in a renter's extended benefit unit`
    `disabled children`                                                                                IS A `Children in a renter's extended benefit unit`
    `persons who may satisfy the overnight care condition`                                              IS A LIST OF `Person who may satisfy the overnight care condition`
    `renters as holders of the foster parent condition`                                                 IS A LIST OF `Renter who may satisfy the foster parent condition`
    `renters as holders of the disabled person condition`                                               IS A LIST OF `Renter who may satisfy the disabled person condition`

-- Paragraph 12(8): as many additional bedrooms as are necessary to ensure that each child with the disabled child condition has their own.
-- The number needed is the number of such children, plus the fewest bedrooms for all the others, less the fewest bedrooms for all the children together.
-- src:2302 | (8) Where a renter, or one or both of joint renters, satisfy the disabled child condition in relation to one or more children, they are entitled to as many additional bedrooms as are necessary to ensure that each such child has their own bedroom.
@ref Sch 4 para 12(8) (src:2302)
GIVEN unit IS A `Extended benefit unit for the size criteria`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Sch 4 para 12(8) — the additional bedrooms for the disabled child condition` unit MEANS
    max 0 (    (`Sch 4 para 10(1)(d) to (f) — the number of children in a group` (unit's `disabled children`))
           PLUS (`Sch 4 para 10(2) — the fewest bedrooms for a group of children` (`Sch 4 para 12(8) — the children who are left when the children with the disabled child condition are taken out` (unit's children) (unit's `disabled children`)))
           MINUS (`Sch 4 para 10(2) — the fewest bedrooms for a group of children` (unit's children)))

-- Paragraph 12(6): the disabled child condition is satisfied when a child with it would, but for paragraph 12, be expected to share.
-- Read as: giving each such child their own bedroom needs at least one bedroom more (fork U3-F11).
-- src:2286 | (6) A renter satisfies the disabled child condition if they or another member of their extended benefit unit are responsible for a child who would (but for the provisions of this paragraph) be expected to share a bedroom and that child is—
-- src:2287 | (a) in receipt of—
-- src:2288 | (i) the care component of disability living allowance at the middle or highest rate; or
-- src:2289 | (ii) the care component of child disability payment at the middle or highest rate in accordance with regulation 11(5) of the DACYP Regulations; and
-- src:2290 | (b) by virtue of their disability, not reasonably able to share a room with another child.
@ref Sch 4 para 12(6) (src:2286-2290)
GIVEN unit IS A `Extended benefit unit for the size criteria`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 4 para 12(6) — the renter satisfies the disabled child condition` unit MEANS
    `Sch 4 para 12(8) — the additional bedrooms for the disabled child condition` unit AT LEAST 1

-- src:2261 | (A1) A renter is entitled to an additional bedroom if one or more of the following persons satisfies the overnight care condition (see sub-paragraph (3))—
-- src:2262 | (a) the renter;
-- src:2263 | (b) a person in the renter’s extended benefit unit;
-- src:2264 | (c) a child in respect of whom the renter satisfies the foster parent condition (see sub-paragraphs (4) and (5)).
@ref Sch 4 para 12(A1) (src:2261-2264)
GIVEN unit IS A `Extended benefit unit for the size criteria`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Sch 4 para 12(A1) — the additional bedroom for the overnight care condition` unit MEANS
    IF `Sch 4 para 12(A1) — one or more of the persons listed satisfies the overnight care condition` (unit's `persons who may satisfy the overnight care condition`) THEN 1 ELSE 0

-- src:2305 | (b) the renter, or one or both of joint renters, satisfies the foster parent condition;
@ref Sch 4 para 12(9)(b) (src:2305)
GIVEN unit IS A `Extended benefit unit for the size criteria`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Sch 4 para 12(9)(b) — the additional bedroom for the foster parent condition` unit MEANS
    IF any `Sch 4 para 12(4) — a renter satisfies the foster parent condition` (unit's `renters as holders of the foster parent condition`) THEN 1 ELSE 0

-- src:2307 | (d) the renter, or one or both of joint renters, satisfies the disabled person condition.
@ref Sch 4 para 12(9)(d) (src:2307)
GIVEN unit IS A `Extended benefit unit for the size criteria`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Sch 4 para 12(9)(d) — the additional bedroom for the disabled person condition` unit MEANS
    IF any `Sch 4 para 12(6A) — a renter satisfies the disabled person condition` (unit's `renters as holders of the disabled person condition`) THEN 1 ELSE 0

-- Paragraph 12(9): the additional bedrooms in all (the disabled child condition counts as many as paragraph 12(8) makes necessary).
-- src:2302 | (8) Where a renter, or one or both of joint renters, satisfy the disabled child condition in relation to one or more children, they are entitled to as many additional bedrooms as are necessary to ensure that each such child has their own bedroom.
-- src:2303 | (9) The renter is, or joint renters are, entitled to one additional bedroom for each of the following that apply—
-- src:2304 | (a) one or more persons satisfy the overnight care condition;
-- src:2305 | (b) the renter, or one or both of joint renters, satisfies the foster parent condition;
-- src:2306 | (c) the renter, or one or both of joint renters, satisfies the disabled child condition; or
-- src:2307 | (d) the renter, or one or both of joint renters, satisfies the disabled person condition.
@ref Sch 4 para 12(8) and (9) (src:2302-2307)
GIVEN unit IS A `Extended benefit unit for the size criteria`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Sch 4 para 12 — the additional bedrooms` unit MEANS
    (`Sch 4 para 12(A1) — the additional bedroom for the overnight care condition` unit)
    PLUS (`Sch 4 para 12(9)(b) — the additional bedroom for the foster parent condition` unit)
    PLUS (`Sch 4 para 12(8) — the additional bedrooms for the disabled child condition` unit)
    PLUS (`Sch 4 para 12(9)(d) — the additional bedroom for the disabled person condition` unit)

-- Paragraph 10(1): one bedroom for the renter (or the joint renters together), one for each qualifying young person, one for each
-- non-dependant who is not a child, and the fewest bedrooms that the children can be allotted to under (d) to (f) and (2).
-- src:2228 | (1) A renter is entitled to one bedroom for each of the following categories of persons in their extended benefit unit—
-- src:2229 | (a) the renter (or joint renters);
-- src:2230 | (b) a qualifying young person for whom the renter or either joint renter is responsible;
-- src:2231 | (c) a non-dependant who is not a child;
-- src:2232 | (d) two children who are under 10 years old;
-- src:2233 | (e) two children of the same sex;
-- src:2234 | (f) any other child.
-- src:2235 | (2) A member of the extended benefit unit to whom two or more of the descriptions in sub-paragraph (1) apply is to be allotted to whichever description results in the renter being entitled to the fewest bedrooms.
@ref Sch 4 para 10(1) and (2) (src:2228-2235)
GIVEN unit IS A `Extended benefit unit for the size criteria`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Sch 4 para 10(1) — the bedrooms before any additional bedroom` unit MEANS
    1
    PLUS (unit's `qualifying young persons for whom the renter or either joint renter is responsible`)
    PLUS (unit's `non-dependants who are not children`)
    PLUS (`Sch 4 para 10(2) — the fewest bedrooms for a group of children` (unit's children))

-- Paragraph 10(3): the entitlement takes in paragraph 12's additional bedrooms (and, in Part 4, paragraphs 26 to 29).
-- src:2236 | (3) In determining the number of bedrooms to which a renter is entitled, the following must also be taken into account—
-- src:2237 | (a) the provisions of paragraph 11 as to treatment of periods of temporary absence of members of the renter's extended benefit unit;
-- src:2238 | (b) any entitlement to an additional bedroom in accordance with paragraph 12;
-- src:2239 | (c) for the purpose of any calculation under Part 4 of this Schedule, the additional requirements in paragraphs 26 to 29.
@ref Sch 4 para 10(3)(a) and (b) (src:2236-2238)
GIVEN unit IS A `Extended benefit unit for the size criteria`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Sch 4 para 10 — the number of bedrooms to which a renter is entitled` unit MEANS
    (`Sch 4 para 10(1) — the bedrooms before any additional bedroom` unit)
    PLUS (`Sch 4 para 12 — the additional bedrooms` unit)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Paragraph 26 (Part 4 only): no renter is entitled to more than 4 bedrooms.
-- src:2469 | 26 Four bedroom limit
-- src:2470 | In calculating the amount of a renter's housing costs element under paragraph 22, no renter is entitled to more than 4 bedrooms.
@ref Sch 4 para 26 (src:2469-2470)
GIVEN unit IS A `Extended benefit unit for the size criteria`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Sch 4 para 26 — the number of bedrooms to which a renter is entitled under Part 4` unit MEANS
    min 4 (`Sch 4 para 10 — the number of bedrooms to which a renter is entitled` unit)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Paragraph 29(10), "hostel": a building (a) with domestic accommodation that is not separate and self-contained, and board or food
-- preparation facilities adequate to the needs of those persons or both; (b) managed or owned by one of three kinds of body; and (c) not a care home.
-- src:2514 | “hostel” means a building—
-- src:2515 | (a) in which there is provided, for persons generally or for a class of persons, domestic accommodation, otherwise than in separate and self-contained premises, and either board or facilities for the preparation of food adequate to the needs of those persons, or both; and
-- src:2516 | (b) which—
-- src:2517 | (i) is managed or owned by a provider of social housing other than a local authority, or
-- src:2518 | (ii) is operated other than on a commercial basis and in respect of which funds are provided wholly or in part by a government department or agency or a local authority, or
-- src:2519 | (iii) is managed by a voluntary organisation or a registered charity and provides care, support or supervision with a view to assisting those persons to be rehabilitated or resettled within the community; and
-- src:2520 | (c) which is not a care home;
@ref Sch 4 para 29(10) "hostel" (src:2514-2520)
DECLARE `Building that may be a hostel` HAS
    `domestic accommodation is provided for persons generally or for a class of persons otherwise than in separate and self-contained premises`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `board is provided`                                                                                      IS A BOOLEAN
    `facilities for the preparation of food adequate to the needs of those persons are provided`            IS A BOOLEAN
    `the owner or manager as a possible provider of social housing`                                         IS A `Landlord that may be a provider of social housing`
    `the building is operated other than on a commercial basis`                                            IS A BOOLEAN
    `funds are provided wholly or in part by a government department or agency or a local authority`       IS A BOOLEAN
    `the manager as a possible voluntary organisation`                                                      IS A `Body that may be a voluntary organisation`
    `the manager as a possible registered charity`                                                          IS A `Charity that may be a registered charity`
    `the building provides care, support or supervision with a view to assisting those persons to be rehabilitated or resettled within the community`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the building as possible care home premises`                                                           IS A `Premises that may be a care home`

-- src:2515 | (a) in which there is provided, for persons generally or for a class of persons, domestic accommodation, otherwise than in separate and self-contained premises, and either board or facilities for the preparation of food adequate to the needs of those persons, or both; and
@ref Sch 4 para 29(10) "hostel" (a) (src:2515)
GIVEN building IS A `Building that may be a hostel`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 4 para 29(10) — hostel, limb (a)` building MEANS
    (building's `domestic accommodation is provided for persons generally or for a class of persons otherwise than in separate and self-contained premises`)
    AND ((building's `board is provided`) OR (building's `facilities for the preparation of food adequate to the needs of those persons are provided`))

-- src:2517 | (i) is managed or owned by a provider of social housing other than a local authority, or
@ref Sch 4 para 29(10) "hostel" (b)(i) (src:2517)
GIVEN building IS A `Building that may be a hostel`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 4 para 29(10) — hostel, limb (b)(i)` building MEANS
    (`Sch 4 para 2 — provider of social housing` (building's `the owner or manager as a possible provider of social housing`))
    AND (NOT (`reg 2 — local authority` ((building's `the owner or manager as a possible provider of social housing`)'s `the landlord as a possible local authority`)))

-- src:2518 | (ii) is operated other than on a commercial basis and in respect of which funds are provided wholly or in part by a government department or agency or a local authority, or
@ref Sch 4 para 29(10) "hostel" (b)(ii) (src:2518)
GIVEN building IS A `Building that may be a hostel`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 4 para 29(10) — hostel, limb (b)(ii)` building MEANS
    (building's `the building is operated other than on a commercial basis`)
    AND (building's `funds are provided wholly or in part by a government department or agency or a local authority`)

-- src:2519 | (iii) is managed by a voluntary organisation or a registered charity and provides care, support or supervision with a view to assisting those persons to be rehabilitated or resettled within the community; and
@ref Sch 4 para 29(10) "hostel" (b)(iii) (src:2519)
GIVEN building IS A `Building that may be a hostel`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 4 para 29(10) — the manager of the building is a voluntary organisation or a registered charity` building MEANS
    (`Sch 1 para 1 — voluntary organisation` (building's `the manager as a possible voluntary organisation`))
    OR (`Sch 1 para 1 — registered charity` (building's `the manager as a possible registered charity`))

-- src:2519 | (iii) is managed by a voluntary organisation or a registered charity and provides care, support or supervision with a view to assisting those persons to be rehabilitated or resettled within the community; and
@ref Sch 4 para 29(10) "hostel" (b)(iii) (src:2519)
GIVEN building IS A `Building that may be a hostel`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 4 para 29(10) — hostel, limb (b)(iii)` building MEANS
    (`Sch 4 para 29(10) — the manager of the building is a voluntary organisation or a registered charity` building)
    AND (building's `the building provides care, support or supervision with a view to assisting those persons to be rehabilitated or resettled within the community`)

-- src:2516 | (b) which—
-- src:2517 | (i) is managed or owned by a provider of social housing other than a local authority, or
-- src:2518 | (ii) is operated other than on a commercial basis and in respect of which funds are provided wholly or in part by a government department or agency or a local authority, or
-- src:2519 | (iii) is managed by a voluntary organisation or a registered charity and provides care, support or supervision with a view to assisting those persons to be rehabilitated or resettled within the community; and
@ref Sch 4 para 29(10) "hostel" (b) (src:2516-2519)
GIVEN building IS A `Building that may be a hostel`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 4 para 29(10) — hostel, limb (b)` building MEANS
    (`Sch 4 para 29(10) — hostel, limb (b)(i)` building)
    OR (`Sch 4 para 29(10) — hostel, limb (b)(ii)` building)
    OR (`Sch 4 para 29(10) — hostel, limb (b)(iii)` building)

-- src:2514 | “hostel” means a building—
-- src:2515 | (a) in which there is provided, for persons generally or for a class of persons, domestic accommodation, otherwise than in separate and self-contained premises, and either board or facilities for the preparation of food adequate to the needs of those persons, or both; and
-- src:2516 | (b) which—
-- src:2517 | (i) is managed or owned by a provider of social housing other than a local authority, or
-- src:2518 | (ii) is operated other than on a commercial basis and in respect of which funds are provided wholly or in part by a government department or agency or a local authority, or
-- src:2519 | (iii) is managed by a voluntary organisation or a registered charity and provides care, support or supervision with a view to assisting those persons to be rehabilitated or resettled within the community; and
-- src:2520 | (c) which is not a care home;
@ref Sch 4 para 29(10) "hostel" (src:2514-2520)
GIVEN building IS A `Building that may be a hostel`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 4 para 29(10) — hostel` building MEANS
    (`Sch 4 para 29(10) — hostel, limb (a)` building)
    AND (`Sch 4 para 29(10) — hostel, limb (b)` building)
    AND (NOT (`Sch 1 para 1 — care home` (building's `the building as possible care home premises`)))

-- "Hostel for homeless people": a hostel whose main purpose is to provide accommodation together with care, support or supervision for homeless
-- people with a view to assisting them to be rehabilitated or resettled within the community.
-- src:2521 | “hostel for homeless people” means a hostel the main purpose of which is to provide accommodation together with care, support or supervision for homeless people with a view to assisting such persons to be rehabilitated or resettled within the community.
@ref Sch 4 para 29(10) "hostel for homeless people" (src:2521)
DECLARE `Building that may be a hostel for homeless people` HAS
    `the building as a possible hostel`                                                                                IS A `Building that may be a hostel`
    `the main purpose of the building is to provide accommodation together with care, support or supervision for homeless people with a view to assisting such persons to be rehabilitated or resettled within the community`  IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:2521 | “hostel for homeless people” means a hostel the main purpose of which is to provide accommodation together with care, support or supervision for homeless people with a view to assisting such persons to be rehabilitated or resettled within the community.
@ref Sch 4 para 29(10) "hostel for homeless people" (src:2521)
GIVEN building IS A `Building that may be a hostel for homeless people`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 4 para 29(10) — hostel for homeless people` building MEANS
    (`Sch 4 para 29(10) — hostel` (building's `the building as a possible hostel`))
    AND (building's `the main purpose of the building is to provide accommodation together with care, support or supervision for homeless people with a view to assisting such persons to be rehabilitated or resettled within the community`)

-- Paragraph 29(10), "person acting in an official capacity": one of five descriptions.
-- src:2522 | “person acting in an official capacity” means a health care professional (within the meaning given by regulation 98(4)), a police officer, a registered social worker (within the meaning given by regulation 98(4)), the victim’s employer, or any public, voluntary, or charitable body which has had direct contact with the victim in connection with domestic violence;
@ref Sch 4 para 29(10) "person acting in an official capacity" (src:2522)
DECLARE `Person who may be a person acting in an official capacity` HAS
    -- out of range: reg 98(4) (piece uc4), "health care professional"
    `health care professional within the meaning given by regulation 98(4)`                                             IS A BOOLEAN
    `police officer`                                                                                                    IS A BOOLEAN
    -- out of range: reg 98(4) (piece uc4), "registered social worker"
    `registered social worker within the meaning given by regulation 98(4)`                                             IS A BOOLEAN
    `the victim's employer`                                                                                             IS A BOOLEAN
    `a public, voluntary, or charitable body which has had direct contact with the victim in connection with domestic violence`  IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:2522 | “person acting in an official capacity” means a health care professional (within the meaning given by regulation 98(4)), a police officer, a registered social worker (within the meaning given by regulation 98(4)), the victim’s employer, or any public, voluntary, or charitable body which has had direct contact with the victim in connection with domestic violence;
@ref Sch 4 para 29(10) "person acting in an official capacity" (src:2522)
GIVEN person IS A `Person who may be a person acting in an official capacity`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 4 para 29(10) — person acting in an official capacity` person MEANS
    (person's `health care professional within the meaning given by regulation 98(4)`)
    OR (person's `police officer`)
    OR (person's `registered social worker within the meaning given by regulation 98(4)`)
    OR (person's `the victim's employer`)
    OR (person's `a public, voluntary, or charitable body which has had direct contact with the victim in connection with domestic violence`)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Paragraph 29: the excepted person, "E". Every limb after (2) opens with an age bound; (6) to (9) are tied to a nation of Great Britain.
-- The nation to which E is related is the nation E's accommodation is in (fork U3-F12, assumed and not ruled): the text says only "in relation to".
-- src:2482 | (1) “Excepted person” means any renter (“E”) who falls within any of sub-paragraphs (2) to (9C).
@ref Sch 4 para 29(1) (src:2482)
DECLARE `Stay in a hostel` HAS
    `the hostel`                                                                                      IS A `Building that may be a hostel for homeless people`
    `months the stay lasted`                                                                          IS A NUMBER
    `whilst living in the hostel E was offered and has accepted services which the Secretary of State considers are intended to assist E to be rehabilitated or resettled within the community`  IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:2482 | (1) “Excepted person” means any renter (“E”) who falls within any of sub-paragraphs (2) to (9C).
@ref Sch 4 para 29(1) (src:2482)
DECLARE `Renter who may be an excepted person` HAS
    `age in complete years`                                                                           IS A NUMBER
    `nation of Great Britain to which the renter is related`                                         IS A `Nation of Great Britain`
    -- out of range: reg 8 (piece uc1), "care leaver"
    `was a care leaver within the meaning of regulation 8 before reaching the age of 18`             IS A BOOLEAN
    `stays in hostels`                                                                                IS A LIST OF `Stay in a hostel`
    payments                                                                                          IS A `Disability payments of a person`
    `active multi-agency management pursuant to arrangements established by a responsible authority under section 325(2) of the Criminal Justice Act 2003`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `active multi-agency risk management pursuant to arrangements established by the responsible authorities under section 10(1) of the 2005 Act`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `section 10(1) of the 2005 Act does not apply by reason only of the fact that section 10(1)(b) or (d) has not been brought fully into force`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `section 10(1) of the 2005 Act does not apply by reason only of the fact that section 10(1)(e) has not been brought fully into force`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `considered by the Secretary of State to be a person who may cause serious harm to the public at large`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `by reason of an offence of which they have been convicted, considered by the Secretary of State to be a person who may cause serious harm to the public at large`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the renter as a possible holder of the foster parent condition`                                  IS A `Renter who may satisfy the foster parent condition`
    `after attaining the age of 16 had domestic violence inflicted upon or threatened against them by their partner or former partner, or by a relative`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person who provides evidence that the circumstances are consistent with domestic violence having been inflicted or threatened`  IS A `Person who may be a person acting in an official capacity`
    `the victim's circumstances are consistent with their having had domestic violence inflicted upon or threatened against them`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person whom the victim has contacted in relation to such an incident`                       IS A `Person who may be a person acting in an official capacity`
    `a competent authority has determined that the renter is a victim of trafficking in human beings, slavery, servitude or forced or compulsory labour`  IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:2483 | (2) E is at least 18 but under 25 years old and was a care leaver (within the meaning of regulation 8) before reaching the age of 18.
@ref Sch 4 para 29(2) (src:2483)
GIVEN renter IS A `Renter who may be an excepted person`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 4 para 29(2) — E is at least 18 but under 25 and was a care leaver` renter MEANS
    (renter's `age in complete years` AT LEAST 18)
    AND (renter's `age in complete years` LESS THAN 25)
    AND (renter's `was a care leaver within the meaning of regulation 8 before reaching the age of 18`)

-- Months of stay in hostels for homeless people: the sum of the months of the stays whose hostel is one.
-- src:2485 | (a) has, for a total of at least 3 months (whether or not continuously), lived in one or more hostels for homeless people; and
@ref Sch 4 para 29(4)(a) (src:2485)
GIVEN renter IS A `Renter who may be an excepted person`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Sch 4 para 29(4)(a) — the months E has lived in hostels for homeless people` renter MEANS
    sum (map (GIVEN stay YIELD IF `Sch 4 para 29(10) — hostel for homeless people` (stay's `the hostel`) THEN stay's `months the stay lasted` ELSE 0) (renter's `stays in hostels`))

-- src:2484 | (4) E is at least 16 but under 35 years old and—
-- src:2485 | (a) has, for a total of at least 3 months (whether or not continuously), lived in one or more hostels for homeless people; and
-- src:2486 | (b) whilst E was living in such a hostel, was offered and has accepted services which the Secretary of State considers are intended to assist E to be rehabilitated or resettled within the community.
@ref Sch 4 para 29(4) (src:2484-2486)
GIVEN renter IS A `Renter who may be an excepted person`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 4 para 29(4) — E is at least 16 but under 35 and has lived in hostels and accepted services` renter MEANS
    (renter's `age in complete years` AT LEAST 16)
    AND (renter's `age in complete years` LESS THAN 35)
    AND (`Sch 4 para 29(4)(a) — the months E has lived in hostels for homeless people` renter AT LEAST 3)
    AND (any (GIVEN stay YIELD (`Sch 4 para 29(10) — hostel for homeless people` (stay's `the hostel`)) AND (stay's `whilst living in the hostel E was offered and has accepted services which the Secretary of State considers are intended to assist E to be rehabilitated or resettled within the community`)) (renter's `stays in hostels`))

-- src:2487 | (5) E is under 35 years old and is in receipt of—
-- src:2488 | (a) the care component of disability living allowance at the middle or highest rate;
-- src:2489 | (aa) the care component of child disability payment at the middle or highest rate in accordance with regulation 11(5) of the DACYP Regulations;
-- src:2490 | (ab) the care component of Scottish adult disability living allowance at the highest or middle rate in accordance with regulation 6(4) of the Disability Assistance (Scottish Adult Disability Living Allowance) Regulations 2025;
-- src:2491 | (b) attendance allowance; ...
-- src:2492 | (c) the daily living component of personal independence payment or;
-- src:2493 | (d) the daily living component of adult disability payment at the standard or enhanced rate
@ref Sch 4 para 29(5) (src:2487-2493)
GIVEN renter IS A `Renter who may be an excepted person`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 4 para 29(5) — E is under 35 and in receipt of a listed payment` renter MEANS
    (renter's `age in complete years` LESS THAN 35)
    AND (`Sch 4 para 29(5) — a person in receipt of one of the listed payments` (renter's payments))

-- src:2494 | (6) In relation to England and Wales, E is under 35 years old and is the subject of active multi-agency management pursuant to arrangements established by a responsible authority under section 325(2) of the Criminal Justice Act 2003 (arrangements for assessing etc. risks posed by certain offenders) .
@ref Sch 4 para 29(6) (src:2494)
GIVEN renter IS A `Renter who may be an excepted person`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 4 para 29(6) — in England and Wales, E is under 35 and subject to active multi-agency management` renter MEANS
    (renter's `age in complete years` LESS THAN 35)
    AND (CONSIDER renter's `nation of Great Britain to which the renter is related`
         WHEN England  THEN TRUE
         WHEN Wales    THEN TRUE
         WHEN Scotland THEN FALSE)
    AND (renter's `active multi-agency management pursuant to arrangements established by a responsible authority under section 325(2) of the Criminal Justice Act 2003`)

-- src:2495 | (7) In relation to Scotland, E is under 35 years old and is the subject of active multi-agency risk management pursuant to arrangements established by the responsible authorities under section 10(1) of the 2005 Act (arrangements for assessing and managing risks posed by certain offenders).
@ref Sch 4 para 29(7) (src:2495)
GIVEN renter IS A `Renter who may be an excepted person`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 4 para 29(7) — in Scotland, E is under 35 and subject to active multi-agency risk management` renter MEANS
    (renter's `age in complete years` LESS THAN 35)
    AND (CONSIDER renter's `nation of Great Britain to which the renter is related`
         WHEN England  THEN FALSE
         WHEN Wales    THEN FALSE
         WHEN Scotland THEN TRUE)
    AND (renter's `active multi-agency risk management pursuant to arrangements established by the responsible authorities under section 10(1) of the 2005 Act`)

-- src:2496 | (8) In relation to Scotland, E is under 35 years old and—
-- src:2497 | (a) section 10(1) of the 2005 Act does not apply to E by reason only of the fact that section 10(1)(b) or (d) has not been brought fully into force; and
-- src:2498 | (b) E is considered by the Secretary of State to be a person who may cause serious harm to the public at large.
@ref Sch 4 para 29(8) (src:2496-2498)
GIVEN renter IS A `Renter who may be an excepted person`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 4 para 29(8) — in Scotland, E is under 35 and section 10(1)(b) or (d) is not fully in force` renter MEANS
    (renter's `age in complete years` LESS THAN 35)
    AND (CONSIDER renter's `nation of Great Britain to which the renter is related`
         WHEN England  THEN FALSE
         WHEN Wales    THEN FALSE
         WHEN Scotland THEN TRUE)
    AND (renter's `section 10(1) of the 2005 Act does not apply by reason only of the fact that section 10(1)(b) or (d) has not been brought fully into force`)
    AND (renter's `considered by the Secretary of State to be a person who may cause serious harm to the public at large`)

-- src:2499 | (9) In relation to Scotland, E is under 35 years old and—
-- src:2500 | (a) section 10(1) of the 2005 Act does not apply to E by reason only of the fact that section 10(1)(e) has not been brought fully into force; and
-- src:2501 | (b) by reason of an offence of which E has been convicted, E is considered by the Secretary of State to be a person who may cause serious harm to the public at large.
@ref Sch 4 para 29(9) (src:2499-2501)
GIVEN renter IS A `Renter who may be an excepted person`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 4 para 29(9) — in Scotland, E is under 35 and section 10(1)(e) is not fully in force` renter MEANS
    (renter's `age in complete years` LESS THAN 35)
    AND (CONSIDER renter's `nation of Great Britain to which the renter is related`
         WHEN England  THEN FALSE
         WHEN Wales    THEN FALSE
         WHEN Scotland THEN TRUE)
    AND (renter's `section 10(1) of the 2005 Act does not apply by reason only of the fact that section 10(1)(e) has not been brought fully into force`)
    AND (renter's `by reason of an offence of which they have been convicted, considered by the Secretary of State to be a person who may cause serious harm to the public at large`)

-- src:2502 | (9A) E is under 35 years old and satisfies the foster parent condition (within the meaning of paragraph 12(4)).
@ref Sch 4 para 29(9A) (src:2502)
GIVEN renter IS A `Renter who may be an excepted person`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 4 para 29(9A) — E is under 35 and satisfies the foster parent condition` renter MEANS
    (renter's `age in complete years` LESS THAN 35)
    AND (`Sch 4 para 12(4) — a renter satisfies the foster parent condition` (renter's `the renter as a possible holder of the foster parent condition`))

-- src:2503 | (9B) E is under 35 years old and—
-- src:2504 | (a) after attaining the age of 16 had domestic violence inflicted upon or threatened against them (“the victim”) by their partner or former partner, or by a relative; and
-- src:2505 | (b) provides evidence from a person acting in an official capacity which demonstrates that—
-- src:2506 | (i) the victim’s circumstances are consistent with their having had domestic violence inflicted upon or threatened against them; and
-- src:2507 | (ii) the victim has contacted a person acting in an official capacity in relation to such an incident.
@ref Sch 4 para 29(9B) (src:2503-2507)
GIVEN renter IS A `Renter who may be an excepted person`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 4 para 29(9B) — E is under 35 and has had domestic violence inflicted or threatened, with evidence` renter MEANS
    (renter's `age in complete years` LESS THAN 35)
    AND (renter's `after attaining the age of 16 had domestic violence inflicted upon or threatened against them by their partner or former partner, or by a relative`)
    AND (`Sch 4 para 29(10) — person acting in an official capacity` (renter's `the person who provides evidence that the circumstances are consistent with domestic violence having been inflicted or threatened`))
    AND (renter's `the victim's circumstances are consistent with their having had domestic violence inflicted upon or threatened against them`)
    AND (`Sch 4 para 29(10) — person acting in an official capacity` (renter's `the person whom the victim has contacted in relation to such an incident`))

-- src:2508 | (9C) E is under 35 years old and has been the subject of a positive conclusive grounds determination relating to modern slavery.
@ref Sch 4 para 29(9C) (src:2508)
GIVEN renter IS A `Renter who may be an excepted person`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 4 para 29(9C) — E is under 35 and has been the subject of a positive conclusive grounds determination` renter MEANS
    (renter's `age in complete years` LESS THAN 35)
    AND (renter's `a competent authority has determined that the renter is a victim of trafficking in human beings, slavery, servitude or forced or compulsory labour`)

-- src:2482 | (1) “Excepted person” means any renter (“E”) who falls within any of sub-paragraphs (2) to (9C).
@ref Sch 4 para 29(1) (src:2482)
GIVEN renter IS A `Renter who may be an excepted person`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 4 para 29(1) — an excepted person` renter MEANS
    (`Sch 4 para 29(2) — E is at least 18 but under 25 and was a care leaver` renter)
    OR (`Sch 4 para 29(4) — E is at least 16 but under 35 and has lived in hostels and accepted services` renter)
    OR (`Sch 4 para 29(5) — E is under 35 and in receipt of a listed payment` renter)
    OR (`Sch 4 para 29(6) — in England and Wales, E is under 35 and subject to active multi-agency management` renter)
    OR (`Sch 4 para 29(7) — in Scotland, E is under 35 and subject to active multi-agency risk management` renter)
    OR (`Sch 4 para 29(8) — in Scotland, E is under 35 and section 10(1)(b) or (d) is not fully in force` renter)
    OR (`Sch 4 para 29(9) — in Scotland, E is under 35 and section 10(1)(e) is not fully in force` renter)
    OR (`Sch 4 para 29(9A) — E is under 35 and satisfies the foster parent condition` renter)
    OR (`Sch 4 para 29(9B) — E is under 35 and has had domestic violence inflicted or threatened, with evidence` renter)
    OR (`Sch 4 para 29(9C) — E is under 35 and has been the subject of a positive conclusive grounds determination` renter)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Paragraph 28: the specified renter. First condition: a single person (or a member of a couple claiming as a single person) under 35
-- who is not an excepted person. Second: not responsible for any children or qualifying young persons. Third: no non-dependant.
-- src:2475 | (1) For the purposes of paragraph 27, “specified renter” means a renter in respect of whom all of the following conditions are met.
-- src:2476 | (2) The first condition is that the renter is a single person (or a member of a couple claiming as a single person) who—
-- src:2477 | (a) is under 35 years old; and
-- src:2478 | (b) is not an excepted person under paragraph 29.
-- src:2479 | (3) The second condition is that the renter is not responsible for any children or qualifying young persons.
-- src:2480 | (4) The third condition is that no person is a non-dependant in relation to the renter.
@ref Sch 4 para 28 (src:2475-2480)
DECLARE `Renter who may be a specified renter` HAS
    `claim basis`                                                                                     IS A `Claim basis`
    `the renter as a possible excepted person`                                                         IS A `Renter who may be an excepted person`
    -- out of range: reg 4 (piece uc1), "responsible for a child or qualifying young person"
    `the renter is responsible for any children or qualifying young persons`                          IS A BOOLEAN
    `any person is a non-dependant in relation to the renter`                                         IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:2476 | (2) The first condition is that the renter is a single person (or a member of a couple claiming as a single person) who—
-- src:2477 | (a) is under 35 years old; and
-- src:2478 | (b) is not an excepted person under paragraph 29.
@ref Sch 4 para 28(2) (src:2476-2478)
GIVEN renter IS A `Renter who may be a specified renter`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 4 para 28(2) — the first condition` renter MEANS
    (NOT ((renter's `claim basis`) EQUALS `joint claimants`))
    AND ((renter's `the renter as a possible excepted person`)'s `age in complete years` LESS THAN 35)
    AND (NOT (`Sch 4 para 29(1) — an excepted person` (renter's `the renter as a possible excepted person`)))

-- src:2475 | (1) For the purposes of paragraph 27, “specified renter” means a renter in respect of whom all of the following conditions are met.
-- src:2476 | (2) The first condition is that the renter is a single person (or a member of a couple claiming as a single person) who—
-- src:2477 | (a) is under 35 years old; and
-- src:2478 | (b) is not an excepted person under paragraph 29.
-- src:2479 | (3) The second condition is that the renter is not responsible for any children or qualifying young persons.
-- src:2480 | (4) The third condition is that no person is a non-dependant in relation to the renter.
@ref Sch 4 para 28(1) (src:2475-2480)
GIVEN renter IS A `Renter who may be a specified renter`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 4 para 28(1) — a specified renter` renter MEANS
    (`Sch 4 para 28(2) — the first condition` renter)
    AND (NOT (renter's `the renter is responsible for any children or qualifying young persons`))
    AND (NOT (renter's `any person is a non-dependant in relation to the renter`))

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Paragraph 27: a specified renter is entitled to shared accommodation only. Shared accommodation is the category in paragraph 1(a) of
-- Schedule 1 to the Rent Officers Order 2013, which is not among the inputs; the other categories are those that paragraph 22 reads by bedrooms.
-- src:2472 | (1) In calculating the amount of a renter's housing costs element under paragraph 22, any specified renter (within the meaning of paragraph 28) is entitled to shared accommodation only.
-- src:2473 | (2) “Shared accommodation” means the category of accommodation specified in paragraph 1(a) of Schedule 1 to the Rent Officers Order 2013.
@ref Sch 4 para 27 (src:2472-2473)
DECLARE `Category of accommodation` IS ONE OF
    `shared accommodation`
    `accommodation of a size given by a number of bedrooms` HAS `number of bedrooms` IS A NUMBER

-- src:2472 | (1) In calculating the amount of a renter's housing costs element under paragraph 22, any specified renter (within the meaning of paragraph 28) is entitled to shared accommodation only.
@ref Sch 4 para 27(1) (src:2472)
GIVEN specified IS A BOOLEAN
      unit IS A `Extended benefit unit for the size criteria`
GIVETH A `Category of accommodation`
`Sch 4 para 27(1) — the category of accommodation to which a renter is entitled under Part 4` specified unit MEANS
    IF specified
    THEN `shared accommodation`
    ELSE `accommodation of a size given by a number of bedrooms` WITH `number of bedrooms` IS `Sch 4 para 26 — the number of bedrooms to which a renter is entitled under Part 4` unit
